// Per-machine signing for a PHYSICAL iPhone/iPad build, the one build that cannot be ad-hoc
// signed, because iOS only launches an app whose signature has a provisioning profile behind it.
// project.yml points every configuration at this file and reads MAILCAL_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM from it
// for `sdk=iphoneos*`; simulator and macOS builds sign ad-hoc and never look here.
//
// The team id stays out of git (per-machine, like clients/apple/signing.local.sh) so the default
// below is empty: a fresh checkout builds for the simulator and macOS exactly as before, and a
// device build fails with Xcode's "requires a provisioning profile" until the local file exists.
// `Scripts/build-and-run.sh --device` writes it from the team it resolves, which is also what
// makes Xcode's own Run button work, since Xcode cannot run that detection itself.
MAILCAL_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// `#include?`, the optional form, silent when the file is absent.
#include? "signing.local.xcconfig"
